    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Jackson Merrill** remains our premier play; despite facing an elite catcher who dampens his stolen base potential, his combination of a favorable matchup against Zack Littell and a solidified spot in the batting order makes him our safest high-floor producer. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from a platoon advantage against Canning, with his 14% dynamic platoon boost driving him into the elite tier. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite facing a tough arm in Miles; his massive +16% park factor compensation effectively neutralizes the SP skill deficit, ensuring he remains a focal point of our offensive production.\n\nOur deepest roster decisions centered on the outfield, where **Kyle Tucker** (70.83) and **Andy Pages** (64.70) both cleared the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold comfortably. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.95) was the most difficult exclusion from the top-tier starting spots; while his +16% park adjustment is excellent, the combination of facing Bradish and a -7% platoon drag relegated him to the fringes of our marginal category. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Drake Baldwin** still sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Sam Antonacci** (61.66) to provide speed upside against Keider Montero. Owners should note that **Liam Hicks**, **Josh Jung**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker** are currently under \"Lineup Pending\" status; if confirmed orders shift downward in the lineup, we will be forced to re-evaluate their efficiency scores to ensure we aren't burning valuable game caps on sub-optimal plate appearance projections.",
